1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,623
Ava: Imagine changing the number of GPUs halfway through training and getting a different result.
Ava：想象一下，训练到一半改了 GPU 数量，结果也跟着变了。

2
00:00:05,623 --> 00:00:10,190
If you’re testing a new data mixture, how would you know what helped?
如果你在测试新的数据配比，怎么知道究竟是什么起了作用？

3
00:00:10,190 --> 00:00:13,502
Brian: That’s the problem Zephon tackles in TorchTitan.
Brian：这正是 TorchTitan 中的 Zephon 要解决的问题。

4
00:00:13,502 --> 00:00:21,580
It keeps the global batches the same when a run resumes on a different number of GPUs—graphics processing units.
训练任务恢复时，即使 GPU（图形处理器）数量变了，它也能保持全局批次不变。

5
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:24,983
Ava: I thought a data loader just handed out samples.
Ava：我以为数据加载器只是分发样本。

6
00:00:24,983 --> 00:00:29,586
Why would the GPU count change which samples the model sees?
为什么 GPU 数量会影响模型看到哪些样本？

7
00:00:29,586 --> 00:00:33,554
Brian: Many loaders divide the stream among the GPUs they have.
Brian：很多加载器会按现有 GPU 数量分配数据流。

8
00:00:33,554 --> 00:00:38,302
Change that count, and you can change the order after a checkpoint.
数量一变，从检查点恢复后的数据顺序就可能变。

9
00:00:38,302 --> 00:00:41,912
The model then trains on a different sequence.
模型接着训练时，看到的就是另一套序列。

10
00:00:41,912 --> 00:00:45,790
Ava: And that makes a data experiment hard to trust.
Ava：这样一来，数据实验的结果就很难让人信服。

11
00:00:45,790 --> 00:00:52,269
Brian: Exactly. Teams often test a new mixture, filter, tokenizer, or packing method.
Brian：没错。团队经常测试新的数据配比、过滤规则、分词器或打包方法。

12
00:00:52,269 --> 00:00:58,932
That’s an ablation experiment: change something, then see whether it helped.
这就是消融实验：改动一项，再看是否有帮助。

13
00:00:58,932 --> 00:01:03,290
Ava: There’s another cost before the experiment even starts, right?
Ava：实验还没开始，就已经有另一笔成本了，对吧？

14
00:01:03,290 --> 00:01:03,578
Brian: Yes.
Brian：对。

15
00:01:03,578 --> 00:01:10,048
Preparing each version can mean processing the whole corpus offline and saving a new copy.
准备每个版本，可能都要离线处理整个语料库，再保存一份新副本。

16
00:01:10,048 --> 00:01:13,211
A typical training run reads that copy once.
一次典型训练只会读取这份副本一次。

17
00:01:13,211 --> 00:01:19,240
Many experiments don’t improve the model, so that work and storage go to waste.
很多实验并不能改进模型，处理工作和存储空间就白费了。

18
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:25,878
Ava: Agents can launch lots of experiments now. Does that make the data order problem worse?
Ava：现在智能体能启动大量实验。这会让数据顺序问题更严重吗？

19
00:01:25,878 --> 00:01:27,790
Brian: It makes it easier to miss.
Brian：这会让问题更容易被忽略。

20
00:01:27,790 --> 00:01:34,447
An agent might attribute a score change to its data edit when the GPU allocation also changed.
智能体可能把分数变化归因于数据修改，却没发现 GPU 分配也变了。

21
00:01:34,447 --> 00:01:37,772
The article says people can miss that too.
文章说，人也可能忽略这一点。

22
00:01:37,772 --> 00:01:40,906
Ava: So what does Zephon ask me to define?
Ava：那 Zephon 需要我定义什么？

23
00:01:40,906 --> 00:01:44,155
Brian: Three things. Datasets describe the sources.
Brian：三样东西。Datasets 描述数据来源。

24
00:01:44,155 --> 00:01:47,773
A WorkSource plans how they’re mixed and ordered.
WorkSource 规划数据如何混合、如何排序。

25
00:01:47,773 --> 00:01:54,768
Then a Pipeline of operators turns stored samples into the tensors the training loop uses.
然后，Pipeline 中的算子把存储的样本转换成训练循环使用的张量。

26
00:01:54,768 --> 00:01:58,766
Ava: Can you make that concrete without reading me a screen of code?
Ava：能举个具体例子吗？别给我念一整屏代码。

27
00:01:58,766 --> 00:02:02,438
Brian: The article’s example mixes two text datasets.
Brian：文章里的例子混合了两个文本数据集。

28
00:02:02,438 --> 00:02:10,582
The pipeline tokenizes the text, packs it into fixed-length sequences, shuffles it, and makes batches.
Pipeline 会将文本分词、打包成固定长度的序列、打乱顺序，再组成批次。

29
00:02:10,582 --> 00:02:14,764
That processing happens inside the training job.
这些处理都在训练任务中完成。

30
00:02:14,764 --> 00:02:20,274
Ava: So it doesn’t need a saved, preprocessed copy for every experiment.
Ava：所以不用为每个实验都保存一份预处理后的数据。

31
00:02:20,274 --> 00:02:24,140
Brian: Right. It can use CPUs available while the model trains.
Brian：对。它可以利用模型训练期间可用的 CPU。

32
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:31,808
And because the WorkSource is separate, you can change the mixture without rewriting the processing steps.
而且 WorkSource 是独立的，修改数据配比不用重写处理步骤。

33
00:02:31,808 --> 00:02:37,222
Ava: The example uses equal mixture weights. Equal numbers of documents?
Ava：例子里两份数据的混合权重相同。是指文档数量相同吗？

34
00:02:37,222 --> 00:02:40,222
Brian: Equal proportions of tokens, not samples.
Brian：是词元占比相同，不是样本数量相同。

35
00:02:40,222 --> 00:02:46,150
TokenEstimation checks the token-to-byte ratio in a small sample of each dataset.
TokenEstimation 会从每个数据集抽取少量样本，估算词元与字节的比例。

36
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:52,500
It uses that estimate to plan the mixture while the stored data is still raw text.
数据还存储为原始文本时，它就用这个估算值来规划配比。

37
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:52,991
Ava: Got it.
Ava：明白了。

38
00:02:52,991 --> 00:02:59,162
But packing and shuffling on the fly sound tricky if you want to restart elsewhere.
但如果要换个地方恢复训练，实时打包和打乱顺序听起来很棘手。

39
00:02:59,162 --> 00:03:03,792
Brian: They are. Picture a packing bin that’s partly full when you stop.
Brian：确实。想象一下，停止时有个打包容器只装了一部分。

40
00:03:03,792 --> 00:03:07,282
The next output depends on what’s already inside.
下一个输出取决于里面已经装了什么。

41
00:03:07,282 --> 00:03:12,760
You can’t simply look up the next training sequence at an index on disk.
你没法直接按磁盘上的索引找到下一条训练序列。

42
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:15,128
Ava: That’s the stateful pipeline problem.
Ava：这就是有状态 Pipeline 的问题。

43
00:03:15,128 --> 00:03:19,446
How does Zephon keep parallel workers from changing the order?
Zephon 怎么防止并行工作进程改变顺序？

44
00:03:19,446 --> 00:03:22,459
Brian: It separates decisions from expensive work.
Brian：它把决策和耗时的处理分开。

45
00:03:22,459 --> 00:03:30,097
A single-threaded accumulator sees records in order and decides things like which sequences to pack together.
单线程累加器按顺序读取记录，决定哪些序列要打包在一起等事项。

46
00:03:30,097 --> 00:03:34,652
Stateless functions do the costly processing across workers.
耗时的处理则由无状态函数在多个工作进程中完成。

47
00:03:34,652 --> 00:03:38,650
Ava: Workers can finish in any order, though.
Ava：但工作进程可能以任意顺序完成任务。

48
00:03:38,650 --> 00:03:39,318
Brian: They can.
Brian：是的。

49
00:03:39,318 --> 00:03:46,290
Zephon numbers groups of records before sending them out, then restores their order afterward.
Zephon 在分发前给各组记录编号，完成后再恢复原有顺序。

50
00:03:46,290 --> 00:03:49,701
That makes worker count a performance setting.
这样，工作进程数量就成了一个性能参数。

51
00:03:49,701 --> 00:03:53,760
More tokenization workers won’t change the output.
增加分词工作进程也不会改变输出。

52
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:59,894
Ava: So far, that handles workers. What handles a different number of GPUs?
Ava：这解决了工作进程的问题。GPU 数量变了怎么办？

53
00:03:59,894 --> 00:04:02,649
Brian: Lanes. They’re fixed logical streams.
Brian：靠通道。它们是固定的逻辑数据流。

54
00:04:02,649 --> 00:04:11,188
Each lane has an ordered sample sequence and its own operator state, including any partly filled packing bins.
每条通道都有按顺序排列的样本序列和独立的算子状态，包括尚未装满的打包容器。

55
00:04:11,188 --> 00:04:15,882
Ava: Like numbered conveyor belts that can be assigned to different stations?
Ava：就像编号的传送带，可以分配到不同工位？

56
00:04:15,882 --> 00:04:22,222
Brian: That’s a useful picture. The lane produces the same records whichever GPU gets it.
Brian：这个比喻很贴切。无论分配给哪张 GPU，通道产出的记录都一样。

57
00:04:22,222 --> 00:04:28,330
When the number of data-parallel ranks changes, Zephon redistributes the lanes.
数据并行进程数变化时，Zephon 会重新分配通道。

58
00:04:28,330 --> 00:04:31,232
The global batches stay the same.
全局批次保持不变。

59
00:04:31,232 --> 00:04:40,006
Ava: Let me check I’ve got it: accumulators keep each lane’s decisions in order, and lanes let the run move across GPU counts.
Ava：我确认一下：累加器保证每条通道按顺序决策，通道则让训练能在不同 GPU 数量下运行。

60
00:04:40,006 --> 00:04:45,621
Brian: Exactly. There’s one planning choice: you pick the lane count up front.
Brian：没错。有个规划上的选择：通道数要事先定好。

61
00:04:45,621 --> 00:04:51,348
It needs to divide evenly across the data-parallel sizes you expect.
它必须能被预期使用的各个数据并行规模整除。

62
00:04:51,348 --> 00:04:55,322
Ava: What happens to those partly filled bins at a checkpoint?
Ava：保存检查点时，那些没装满的容器怎么办？

63
00:04:55,322 --> 00:04:59,018
Saving every bit of pipeline state sounds large.
保存流水线的所有状态听起来会很占空间。

64
00:04:59,018 --> 00:05:02,945
Brian: Zephon doesn’t save the bin contents or shuffle buffers.
Brian：Zephon 不保存容器内容或打乱顺序用的缓冲区。

65
00:05:02,945 --> 00:05:07,152
It periodically sends a flush sentinel through the pipeline.
它会定期向流水线发送一个清空哨兵标记。

66
00:05:07,152 --> 00:05:12,832
Stateful operators emit what they’re holding, then start from a clean slate.
有状态的算子会输出暂存的数据，然后从空状态重新开始。

67
00:05:12,832 --> 00:05:15,654
Ava: And when training resumes?
Ava：恢复训练时呢？

68
00:05:15,654 --> 00:05:20,116
Brian: The checkpoint records which input chunks were still in progress.
Brian：检查点会记录哪些输入数据块仍在处理中。

69
00:05:20,116 --> 00:05:28,772
Zephon replays input from the latest flush to rebuild the state, then discards output the training loop already consumed.
Zephon 从最近一次清空的位置重放输入，重建状态，再丢弃训练循环已经用过的输出。

70
00:05:28,772 --> 00:05:32,410
Ava: So replay buys a smaller checkpoint.
Ava：所以重放让检查点变小了。

71
00:05:32,410 --> 00:05:32,674
Brian: Yes.
Brian：对。

72
00:05:32,674 --> 00:05:40,824
In the article’s experiments, those checkpoints were a few MiB—mebibytes—regardless of how far the run had progressed.
文章中的实验里，无论训练进行到哪一步，检查点都只有几 MiB，也就是几兆二进制字节。

73
00:05:40,824 --> 00:05:43,550
Ava: How does this fit into TorchTitan?
Ava：这怎么接入 TorchTitan？

74
00:05:43,550 --> 00:05:51,085
Brian: The integration replaces TorchTitan’s default data loader with a Zephon Pipeline built from a data recipe.
Brian：集成方案用按数据配方构建的 Zephon 流水线替换了 TorchTitan 的默认数据加载器。

75
00:05:51,085 --> 00:05:58,828
The recipe includes datasets, mixture weights, and settings such as packing, shuffling, and parallelism.
配方包括数据集、混合权重，以及打包、打乱顺序和并行度等设置。

76
00:05:58,828 --> 00:06:02,106
Ava: Does the rest of the training run need to change?
Ava：训练的其他部分需要改吗？

77
00:06:02,106 --> 00:06:04,602
Brian: The article says it stays the same.
Brian：文章说不用改。

78
00:06:04,602 --> 00:06:09,310
Zephon’s state goes into the TorchTitan checkpoint with the model.
Zephon 的状态会和模型一起存进 TorchTitan 的检查点。

79
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:15,152
That state covers every lane, so the run can resume on a different GPU count.
状态涵盖每条通道，所以训练可以在不同数量的 GPU 上恢复。

80
00:06:15,152 --> 00:06:18,838
Ava: What if I choose a lane count that doesn’t fit the run?
Ava：如果选的通道数不适合这次训练呢？

81
00:06:18,838 --> 00:06:25,326
Brian: The integration checks at launch that lanes divide evenly across data-parallel replicas.
Brian：集成方案会在启动时检查，通道数能否被数据并行副本数整除。

82
00:06:25,326 --> 00:06:30,855
It also checks that each optimizer step’s batch splits evenly across lanes.
还会检查每次优化器更新的批次能否均分到各通道。

83
00:06:30,855 --> 00:06:33,564
A bad configuration fails early.
配置有误会在启动时立即报错。

84
00:06:33,564 --> 00:06:40,778
Ava: Now for evidence. Did they actually resume a training run with different GPU counts?
Ava：来说说证据。他们真的用不同数量的 GPU 恢复过训练吗？

85
00:06:40,778 --> 00:06:53,800
Brian: They trained a one-billion-parameter model in TorchTitan on sixteen GPUs, checkpointed at step one hundred fifty, then resumed on eight, thirty-two, and sixty-four GPUs, alongside the original run.
Brian：他们在 TorchTitan 上用 16 张 GPU 训练一个 10 亿参数模型，在第 150 步保存检查点，然后分别用 8、32 和 64 张 GPU 恢复训练，并与原训练过程对照。

86
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:56,262
Ava: What did the ordinary loader do?
Ava：普通数据加载器表现如何？

87
00:06:56,262 --> 00:07:00,645
Brian: After the resume, it supplied different sample sequences.
Brian：恢复后，它提供了不同的样本序列。

88
00:07:00,645 --> 00:07:04,916
Each GPU count ended up with a distinct loss curve.
每种 GPU 数量都得到了不同的损失曲线。

89
00:07:04,916 --> 00:07:06,538
Ava: And Zephon?
Ava：Zephon 呢？

90
00:07:06,538 --> 00:07:09,913
Brian: Its loss curves lay on top of each other.
Brian：它的损失曲线完全重合。

91
00:07:09,913 --> 00:07:17,076
The SHA-256 hash—a fingerprint of the data—matched the baseline for every global batch.
每个全局批次的数据指纹，也就是 SHA-256 哈希值，都与基准训练一致。

92
00:07:17,076 --> 00:07:21,048
That checks the batch contents step by step.
这逐步验证了每个批次的内容。

93
00:07:21,048 --> 00:07:26,630
Ava: Matching batches is clear. Did the loader affect evaluation scores too?
Ava：批次一致很明确。数据加载器也影响评测分数吗？

94
00:07:26,630 --> 00:07:35,755
Brian: In another test, they trained the same model from scratch for twenty billion tokens on eight, sixteen, thirty-two, and sixty-four GPUs.
Brian：在另一项测试中，他们分别用 8、16、32 和 64 张 GPU，从头训练同一个模型，处理了 200 亿个词元。

95
00:07:35,755 --> 00:07:42,796
With the standard loader, DCLM Core version one scores varied by up to zero point eight two points.
使用标准数据加载器时，DCLM Core 第一版的得分最多相差 0.82 分。

96
00:07:42,796 --> 00:07:46,482
Ava: What happened on the FineWeb evaluation suite?
Ava：FineWeb 评测套件呢？

97
00:07:46,482 --> 00:07:50,162
Brian: Those scores varied by up to zero point six four points.
Brian：那里的得分最多相差 0.64 分。

98
00:07:50,162 --> 00:08:00,368
The article says these spreads were roughly four times the relevant thresholds used by the DCLM and FineWeb authors to evaluate data curation methods.
文章说，这些分差约为 DCLM 和 FineWeb 作者评估数据筛选方法时所用相应阈值的四倍。

99
00:08:00,368 --> 00:08:07,174
Ava: Wait, so a comparison between data mixtures could pick up the GPU allocation instead?
Ava：等等，也就是说，比较不同数据混合方案时，GPU 的分配也可能影响结果？

100
00:08:07,174 --> 00:08:09,594
Brian: Yes, if the allocations differ.
Brian：对，如果 GPU 分配不同，就可能这样。

101
00:08:09,594 --> 00:08:20,796
With Zephon, the score spreads across GPU counts were zero point zero five on DCLM Core version one and zero point zero one one on FineWeb.
使用 Zephon 时，不同 GPU 数量下的得分差异，在 DCLM Core v1 上为 0.05，在 FineWeb 上为 0.011。

102
00:08:20,796 --> 00:08:25,658
Ava: Does doing all that processing during training slow the GPUs down?
Ava：训练时做这些数据处理，会拖慢 GPU 吗？

103
00:08:25,658 --> 00:08:27,822
Brian: That’s the practical question.
Brian：这正是实际问题。

104
00:08:27,822 --> 00:08:32,078
Zephon lets each operator use its own level of parallelism.
Zephon 允许每个算子采用不同的并行度。

105
00:08:32,078 --> 00:08:38,488
In the example, tokenization gets four workers because it’s the most expensive step.
在这个例子中，分词最耗资源，所以分配了四个工作线程。

106
00:08:38,488 --> 00:08:41,502
Ava: And on a more complex pipeline?
Ava：更复杂的流水线呢？

107
00:08:41,502 --> 00:08:51,879
Brian: On the article’s full vision-language pipeline, which decodes images and then tokenizes, packs, and batches samples, Zephon kept pace with Google Grain.
Brian：在文章的完整视觉语言流水线中，数据要经过图像解码、分词、打包和分批；Zephon 的速度跟上了 Google Grain。

108
00:08:51,879 --> 00:08:55,916
The authors call Grain the fastest loader they tested.
作者称 Grain 是他们测试过最快的数据加载器。

109
00:08:55,916 --> 00:09:01,450
Ava: Does Grain offer the same behavior when a run changes GPU counts?
Ava：运行时改变 GPU 数量，Grain 也能保持同样的表现吗？

110
00:09:01,450 --> 00:09:11,455
Brian: The article says Grain and Mosaic Streaming can preserve global batches across GPU counts when sample order can be worked out ahead of time from an index.
Brian：文章说，如果能通过索引预先确定样本顺序，Grain 和 Mosaic Streaming 就能在不同 GPU 数量下保持全局批次不变。

111
00:09:11,455 --> 00:09:14,664
That condition rules out packing on the fly.
这个条件排除了实时打包。

112
00:09:14,664 --> 00:09:18,854
Ava: And the other loader they mention, Megatron-Energon?
Ava：他们提到的另一个加载器 Megatron-Energon 呢？

113
00:09:18,854 --> 00:09:26,589
Brian: It can reproduce batches with a different number of GPUs if the total number of data loader workers stays the same.
Brian：只要数据加载工作线程总数不变，它就能在 GPU 数量变化后复现批次。

114
00:09:26,589 --> 00:09:30,436
Zephon’s design removes that worker-count condition.
Zephon 的设计不受工作线程数量这个条件限制。

115
00:09:30,436 --> 00:09:33,906
Ava: What should I watch out for when setting up a run?
Ava：设置训练任务时，我该注意什么？

116
00:09:33,906 --> 00:09:37,959
Brian: Choose lanes for the data-parallel sizes you expect.
Brian：根据预计使用的数据并行规模来选择通道数。

117
00:09:37,959 --> 00:09:44,896
The article gives thirty-two lanes as a cap covering eight, sixteen, and thirty-two GPUs.
文章以 32 个通道为上限，覆盖 8、16 和 32 个 GPU 的情况。

118
00:09:44,896 --> 00:09:50,312
Thousands of lanes for a small run can add restore-time overhead.
小规模任务若设置数千个通道，恢复运行时可能增加开销。

119
00:09:50,312 --> 00:09:54,982
Ava: Can I edit the data recipe when I resume on more GPUs?
Ava：用更多 GPU 恢复训练时，我能修改数据配置吗？

120
00:09:54,982 --> 00:10:00,975
Brian: Keep the data, tokenizer, seed, mixture, context length, and global batch size fixed.
Brian：数据、分词器、随机种子、混合比例、上下文长度和全局批次大小都要保持不变。

121
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:05,556
You can still tune performance settings such as parallelism.
并行度等性能参数仍可调整。

122
00:10:05,556 --> 00:10:11,618
Ava: One last distinction: do identical batches mean identical loss values?
Ava：最后区分一下：批次相同，损失值也一定相同吗？

123
00:10:11,618 --> 00:10:13,754
Brian: No. Zephon guarantees the data.
Brian：不一定。Zephon 保证的是数据一致。

124
00:10:13,754 --> 00:10:23,200
Floating-point reductions can happen in a different order when the GPU count changes, so losses should be very close but may differ.
GPU 数量变化后，浮点数归约的顺序可能不同，因此损失值应当非常接近，但可能有差异。

125
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:25,446
Ava: What’s next for the project?
Ava：这个项目接下来有什么计划？

126
00:10:25,446 --> 00:10:32,110
Brian: The authors highlight GIL-free Python, meaning Python without the interpreter lock, and dynamic curricula.
Brian：作者重点提到了无 GIL 的 Python，也就是没有解释器锁的 Python，以及动态课程学习。

127
00:10:32,110 --> 00:10:44,468
They report that a thread-based Zephon runner on Python three point fourteen t fetched vision-language samples about three point seven times faster than its process runner on standard Python.
他们报告称，在 Python 3.14t 上，基于线程的 Zephon 运行器获取视觉语言样本的速度，约为标准 Python 上进程版运行器的 3.7 倍。

128
00:10:44,468 --> 00:10:49,354
Ava: And a dynamic curriculum would change the mixture during training?
Ava：动态课程学习会在训练过程中改变混合比例吗？

129
00:10:49,354 --> 00:10:50,386
Brian: That’s the idea.
Brian：正是这个思路。

130
00:10:50,386 --> 00:10:57,355
Because the WorkSource is separate from the processing Pipeline, it could change mixture weights over a run.
由于 WorkSource 与处理流水线 Pipeline 分离，它可以在运行过程中调整混合权重。

131
00:10:57,355 --> 00:11:03,576
They say they’re working on a configurable component that keeps the determinism guarantees.
他们说，正在开发一个可配置组件，同时保留确定性保证。

132
00:11:03,576 --> 00:11:06,254
Ava: Give me the three-point recap.
Ava：请用三点总结一下。

133
00:11:06,254 --> 00:11:10,142
Brian: First, Zephon prepares data inside the training job.
Brian：第一，Zephon 在训练任务内部准备数据。

134
00:11:10,142 --> 00:11:17,096
Second, ordered accumulators, lanes, and replay keep global batches stable across GPU counts.
第二，有序累加器、通道和重放机制让全局批次在不同 GPU 数量下保持稳定。

135
00:11:17,096 --> 00:11:26,044
Third, keep the recipe fixed when resuming, and remember that matching data doesn’t guarantee identical arithmetic.
第三，恢复训练时保持数据配置不变；数据相同也不保证计算结果完全相同。

136
00:11:26,044 --> 00:11:30,762
Ava: That’s a much cleaner way to test the data. Thanks for listening.
Ava：这样测试数据就清楚多了。感谢收听。
